  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...\n\nExtensive cloud cover today has significantly limited daytime\nheating/instability and therefore the potential for\nthunderstorms have decreased. Still cannot rule out an isolated\nthunderstorm, especially if pockets of clearing develop. Locally\nheavy rainfall/isolated flash flooding still cannot be ruled \nout, but this potential has also decreased.\n\nShowers will gradually end from west to this evening, as the \nfront moves east of the area. This will set the stage for a\nmostly sunny day on Friday with highs in the upper 60s to upper\n70s as high pressure will be in control. Friday night will be\nseasonably chilly with good radiational cooling conditions\npresent. Lows in the 40s are expected Friday night/early\nSaturday morning, but some of the usual colder spots in northern\nOneida County/parts of the Catskills may drop down the mid to\nupper 30s. Patchy frost cannot be ruled out in these locations,\nbut confidence was not high enough at this time to include in\nthe official forecast just yet.\n\nOne more dry day is expected on Saturday with high pressure\nremaining in control. Mostly sunny skies are expected, although\nsome higher clouds may sneak in from the west later in the day\nahead of the next system. Highs on Saturday are expected to be\nin the mid 60s to lower 70s.\n\nKEY MESSAGE 2... \n\nAnother low pressure system will approach from the west \nSaturday night into Sunday, bringing the next round of rain to\nthe area. Southwesterly flow ahead of the low will transport \nmoisture northward, supporting the potential for moderate to \nwidespread rainfall. Showers may continue through much of \nSunday before gradually tapering off by Sunday evening. Monday \ncurrently looks mainly dry as surface high pressure develops \nnorth of the Great Lakes. That being said, some lingering\nshowers will be possible in Northeast PA on Monday.\n\nModel guidance begins to diverge by Tuesday, leading to \nincreasing uncertainity in how the midweek pattern will evolve.\nEither way, the general pattern is looking cool and unsettled,\nbut timing of the scattered rain showers is very uncertain, with\ndry periods in between.",
